        "id": 1882526
      },
      "writtenOn": "2024-03-11T12:26:00Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Won\u0027t this make pvmfw panic for non-Sk use-cases, when `llpvm_changes` is enabled?\n\nWhy not return `Result\u003cOption\u003c...\u003e, ...\u003e` and let the caller decide if they want to abort or not?\n\nFor example, I would expect\n```\nlet fdt \u003d Fdt::create_empty_tree(bytes)?;\nshould_defer_rollback_protection(fdt)\n```\nto return `Ok(false)`, not fail (`Err`).\n\nEmbedding policies like this deep down the callstack increases the risk of logic bugs, IMO.\n\n`None` could be bubbled up back to `main`, which would decide how to handle it, and these FDT-parsing functions (`avf_untrusted_node`, `instance_id`, or even `should_defer_rollback_protection`) could return `libfdt::Result`.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 269,
        "startChar": 8,
        "endLine": 269,
        "endChar": 45
      },
      "revId": "e7bd85d00674fce13f41472b15a9d4ad2e016889",
